    "nominal_timeout": "client.go sets a10-second socket I/O deadline, not a hard wall-duration cap. Request duration includes resumed goroutine scheduling and synchronous response parsing/JSON callbacks.22\u201340second observed durations therefore do not prove equal server service times.",
    "redial": "A transport error closes that VUs socket; the next request redials. tcp_connects increments before Dial and counts attempts, not established connections. Compound-page components may redial immediately before the next think interval.",
    "window_accounting": "Endpoint errors/histograms use request START time for measurement-window inclusion; timeline errors count request COMPLETION time.127989 measured endpoint errors versus206699 all-timeline errors is consistent.",
    "late_sampler": "The sampler advances fixedk against absolute tick deadlines and catches up after a stall. It rotates histograms on actual sampling cadence but labelsT=k-1, so timeline quantiles may be shifted or empty relative to completion counters. Zero quantiles during a stall are not zero-latency service.",
